  "id": "Compound::DB01058 - Gene::1544",
  "verbalization": "Praziquantel's interaction with Cyp1a2 is mediated through a series of interconnected molecular and enzymatic pathways. The evidence suggests that Praziquantel binds to Cyp3a4 and Cyp3a7-cyp3a51p, which are subtypes of the Cyp3a family. These cytochrome P450 enzymes then participate in metabolic activities, including oxidoreduction and aromatase, which are ultimately linked to Cyp1a2. This implies a potential indirect interaction where Praziquantel influences Cyp3a enzymes, which in turn modulate Cyp1a2 activity. The presence of multiple pathways involving Cyp3a subtypes and their participation in diverse metabolic processes highlights a complex, multi-step mechanism by which Praziquantel may affect Cyp1a2. The evidence supports a role for Cyp3a enzymes in the metabolic regulation of Cyp1a2, though the exact nature of this relationship remains partially elucidated.",
